ere blowing  because cardinals coach cliff kingsbury  decided to take a time out  and  after the game he took responsibility  for it he said he wanted to get a look  at what they were going to do he wanted  them to burn their best play for that  spot  and if that was their best play well  they were wrong it was a better play  because that play didn't score the next  play did it was a touchdown pass from  jimmy garoppolo to emmanuel sanders and  emmanuel sanders has been  a great addition he's the guy they  traded for last week third round pick  plus one of those little back end you  give us a five we'll give you a four to  make it look like it's actually being  evened out it basically is a third round  pick  that's a lot to give up for a 32  32 year old receiver who had a torn  achilles tendon late last season but you  know what he's been spectacular so far  and it's just it's clicking now the  passing game is clicking they already  had george kittle need to be a little  worried about him he left the game late  he was on the sidelines he wasn't there  for the final two drives had a knee  injury early kyle shanahan the coach of  the team said after the game that it was  a knee and ankle problem for george  kittle and he did gut it out he had a 30  yard  catch and run for a touchdown after that  knee injury and you could see him take a  helmet to the knee if you're watching on  tv it's one of those moments where the  knee goes in a direction that the knee  is not supposed to go and it looked a  little  serious at first it was surprising to  see him back out there so soon but late  in the game he was standing on the  sidelines and so that's a situation  where he'll get checked out and they may  have to hold their breath a little bit  but they have fought through injury  they're going to get some of their  injured guys back kyle yuschik will be  back for the monday night game most  likely coming up in about 10 days  against the seattle seahawks and the  schedule does ge